{"title":"Career Roadmap · Embedded Engineer","role":"Embedded Engineer","summary":"An Embedded Engineer designs, develops, tests, debugs, and maintains software and hardware systems built into electronic products. Unlike general software development, embedded engineering requires a combination of electronics, programming, microcontrollers, communication protocols, real-time systems, and hardware debugging.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Sc (Bachelor of Science - General / Honours)","Course":"Electronics"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"An Embedded Engineer designs, develops, tests, debugs, and maintains software and hardware systems built into electronic products. Unlike general software development, embedded engineering requires a combination of electronics, programming, microcontrollers, communication protocols, real-time systems, and hardware debugging."},{"type":"p","text":"A B.Sc Electronics graduate has a strong foundation for this career through:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Analog and digital electronics"},{"text":"Electronic circuits"},{"text":"Microprocessors and microcontrollers"},{"text":"Semiconductor fundamentals"},{"text":"Signals and systems"},{"text":"Programming and logical problem-solving"},{"text":"Instrumentation and measurement"},{"text":"The major transition required is from academic electronics to production-grade embedded development."}]},{"type":"h","text":"Strong target profile:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Electronics","C/C++","Microcontrollers","Embedded Systems","RTOS","Communication Protocols","Hardware Debugging","Embedded Linux","IoT"],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Stage","Primary Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"B.Sc Electronics + Embedded Foundation"},{"text":"Electronics, C/C++, microcontrollers, communication p