ngineer","Senior Automotive Engineer","AUTOSAR / Functional Safety Specialist","Automotive Systems Architect"]},{"type":"h","text":"Emerging Technologies"},{"type":"p","text":"The embedded field is moving toward increasingly connected and intelligent devices."},{"type":"p","text":"Important areas to monitor:"},{"type":"h","text":"Edge AI"},{"type":"p","text":"Running machine-learning models directly on devices."},{"type":"flow","items":["Sensor","MCU / Edge Processor","TinyML Model","Local Decision"]},{"type":"h","text":"TinyML"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"TensorFlow Lite Micro concepts"},{"text":"Edge inference"},{"text":"Quantization"},{"text":"Model optimization"},{"text":"Sensor-based ML"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Edge Computing"},{"type":"p","text":"More processing is moving from centralized cloud systems to devices and gateways."},{"type":"h","text":"Matter and Connected Devices"},{"type":"p","text":"Smart-home devices increasingly require interoperable connectivity and secure device ecosystems."},{"type":"h","text":"Digital Twins"},{"type":"p","text":"Embedded devices can increasingly be represented and monitored through digital models."},{"type":"h","text":"Secure IoT"},{"type":"p","text":"Security-by-design, secure boot, signed firmware and secure OTA updates are becoming essential."},{"type":"h","text":"RISC-V"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand the fundamentals of the RISC-V ecosystem and open instruction-set architecture."},{"type":"h","text":"Recommended Final Skill Stack"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Embedded Engineer"},{"text":"│"},{"text":"┌──────────────────┼──────────────────┐"},{"text":"↓ ↓ ↓"},{"text":"Electronics Programming Embedded Systems"},{"text":"│ │ │"},{"text":"Analog/Digital C / C++ MCU"},{"text":"Circuits Python RTOS"},{"text":"Sensors Git Drivers"},{"text":"│ │ │"}]},{"type":"flow","items":["└──────────────────┼──────────────────┘","Communication"]},{"type":"p","text":"│"},{"type":"flow","items":["UART / SPI / I²C / CAN","Debugging Tools"]},{"type":"p","text":"│"},{"type":"flow","items":["GDB / Oscilloscope / Logic Analyzer","Embedded Linux / IoT","Production Embedded Systems"]},{"type":"h","text":"Target Profile by Graduation"},{"type":"p","text":"A strong B.Sc Electronics graduate targeting Embedded Engineering should be able to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Design and understand basic electronic circuits"},{"text":"Program microcontrollers using Embedded C"},{"text":"Work confidently with STM32 or another professional MCU"},{"text":"Configure GPIO, timers, PWM, ADC and interrupts"},{"text":"Communicate with sensors using UART, SPI and I²C"},{"text":"Understand CAN fundamentals"},{"text":"Build RTOS-based applications"},{"text":"Debug firmware using GDB/debug probes"},{"text":"Use oscilloscopes and logic analyzers"},{"text":"Work with Git and professional development workflows"},{"text":"Understand Linux fundamentals"},{"text":"Build at least one IoT-connected embedded system"},{"text":"Read datasheets and reference manuals"},{"text":"Understand hardware-software interaction"},{"text":"Document technical designs and test results"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Ideal Portfolio"},{"type":"p","text":"A graduate portfolio should contain 4–6 strong projects:"},{"type":"table","header":["Project","Skills Demonstrated"],"rows":[[{"text":"STM32 Sensor Controller"},{"text":"Embedded C, GPIO, ADC, I²C"}],[{"text":"RTOS Monitoring System"},{"text":"FreeRTOS, tasks, queues, synchronization"}],[{"text":"CAN Network"},{"text":"CAN, communication, debugging"}],[{"text":"IoT Device"},{"text":"Wi-Fi/BLE, MQTT, cloud"}],[{"text":"Embedded Linux Device"},{"text":"Linux, ARM, drivers"}],[{"text":"TinyML Edge Device"},{"text":"Embedded AI, sensors, inference"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"Each project should include:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Problem Statement","System Architecture","Hardware Block Diagram","Circuit / Components","Firmware Architecture","Source Code","Testing","Debugging